Reviewed `src/blog/people/drafts/Arthur-Mensch.md` and appended a `FRESH EYES REVIEW` block at the bottom. No body edits.

**The two biggest issues:**

1. **The "strongest case against" section avoids the real case against.** In Feb 2024 — months after Mistral lobbied Brussels for AI Act foundation-model concessions *on the grounds that it was Europe's open-source champion* — it took €15M from Microsoft and launched Mistral Large as a closed model on Azure. Green MEPs asked the Commission to investigate whether Mistral had been used as a front for Microsoft's lobbying. That episode is a direct empirical strike on this draft's whole thesis (independence, non-revocability, no foreign vendor holding the switch), and the section argues abstractions instead. The Rabbit Hole even names the exact falsifier — "evidence that the sovereignty argument is downstream of investor and government positioning" — and then never tests it against the one episode that *is* that evidence.

2. **The Type 6 case is all systems he distrusts, no people he trusts.** Alliance density is what separates Six from Five here — two co-founders who were friends of a decade, hires friends first, screens for low ego, assembles France + EU + Nvidia + ASML + Samsung — and it's buried in one Rabbit Hole subtype paragraph. Guillaume Lample and Timothée Lacroix are never named in the body; the draft says "all three co-founders" without telling the reader who the other two are.

Also flagged: three concrete expansions (the neuroimaging→LLM arc as psychology not credential; the Dec 2023 Mixtral magnet-link release, which is the non-revocability thesis as an actual scene; Macron/VivaTech), matching trims to pay for them (body is at 3,852 words against the 3,200–3,900 band), the missing Alexandr Wang cluster link, and an FAQ anchor bug where "How old is Arthur Mensch?" jumps *past* the only place his age appears.

Sources for the two facts I verified: [Euronews on the Microsoft backlash](https://www.euronews.com/2024/02/27/furious-critics-question-microsofts-deal-with-mistral-ai-as-eu-set-to-look-into-it), [Green MEP probe request](https://www.euronews.com/next/2024/03/01/green-meps-ask-eu-to-look-into-ethics-of-mistral-ais-microsoft-partnership), [Corporate Europe Observatory on the AI Act lobbying](https://corporateeurope.org/en/2024/03/trojan-horses-how-european-startups-teamed-big-tech-gut-ai-act), [VentureBeat on the Mixtral torrent drop](https://venturebeat.com/ai/mistral-ai-bucks-release-trend-by-dropping-torrent-link-to-new-open-source-llm).
